Patch crosvm: release display imports of freed scanout buffers.

A guest framebuffer flushed to the Wayland display is imported once (a wl_buffer from a dmabuf, kept in
VirtioGpuResource.display_import). unref_resource dropped the resource without releasing that import, and the
Wayland backend's release_import took (surface_id, import_id) while GpuDisplay passes (import_id, surface_id), so it
removed the wrong entry anyway. The display context holds 64 dmabufs: after the guest compositor had gone through
64 framebuffers (fullscreen video, direct scanout, resizes), every flush failed with "failed to add dmabuf to
context" and the VM's screen froze for good while the guest ran on. Release the import when the guest frees the
resource, and take the arguments in the order the caller passes them.

diff --git a/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs b/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs
index 7592c9b10..d9b01921f 100644
--- a/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs
+++ b/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs
@@ -1066,6 +1066,12 @@ impl VirtioGpu {
             self.rutabaga.unmap(resource_id)?;
         }
 
+        // mothershipOS: free the display's import of a scanout buffer the guest no longer uses (the Wayland
+        // backend keeps 64; leaking them froze the screen once they ran out)
+        if let Some(import_id) = resource.display_import {
+            self.display.borrow_mut().release_import(import_id, 0);
+        }
+
         self.rutabaga.unref_resource(resource_id)?;
         Ok(OkNoData)
     }
diff --git a/gpu_display/src/gpu_display_wl.rs b/gpu_display/src/gpu_display_wl.rs
index d7b16f63b..9409dbeab 100644
--- a/gpu_display/src/gpu_display_wl.rs
+++ b/gpu_display/src/gpu_display_wl.rs
@@ -485,7 +485,7 @@ impl DisplayT for DisplayWl {
         }
     }
 
-    fn release_import(&mut self, _surface_id: u32, import_id: u32) {
+    fn release_import(&mut self, import_id: u32, _surface_id: u32) {	// mothershipOS: as GpuDisplay passes them
         self.dmabufs.remove(&import_id);
     }
 }
